# anodet/ — Reuse, Do Not Rebuild

All project utilities live under `anodet/` and are covered by 63+ green pytest tests. **Never regenerate or duplicate these modules.** Doing so introduces subtle divergence bugs that invalidate experiments without loud failures.

## Key modules (reuse only)
- `anodet/utils/io.py` — atomic JSON, `array_hash`, `frame_hash`, redact
- `anodet/utils/run_metadata.py` — `RunMetadata`, `write_result`, `cell_key`, `is_complete`, `capture_env`
- `anodet/utils/seeding.py`
- `anodet/metrics/metrics.py` — tie-aware AUROC, AUPRC/gain, recall@1%FPR, P@K/R@K, bootstrap
- `anodet/scoring/likelihood.py`, `prompted.py`, `prompted_score.py`
- `anodet/eval/grid.py`, `exp1.py`, `exp2.py`, `exp3_security.py`, `verdict.py`
- `anodet/data/odds.py`, `serialize.py` — `load_odds`, `ODDS_30`
- `anodet/baselines/classical.py` — PyOD IForest/PCA/KNN/ECOD
- `anodet/analysis/aggregate.py`, `stats.py`, `figures.py`

When adding new functionality, extend existing modules or add new files — never copy-paste or rewrite existing ones.
